        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The highest quality proteins are dairy, eggs and meat, with soy the best of the single plant proteins and collagen at the bottom with a score of zero. DIAAS is the better scoring system, but every number on it comes with real study-to-study variation, so treat small differences as noise.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            What matters most is eating enough protein in total, spread across your day. Use quality as a tiebreaker: pick a high-scoring powder if you rely on shakes, are older or are eating less, and if you go plant-based, choose a blend and a slightly bigger scoop.
          </p>
